Subject: [PATCH 07984/11362] [outer-loop] lever2: populate the HUD diagnostics
 FLAT on the scored path

THE DEFECT (measured, not inferred). hud_mask_resolved / hud_mask_cell_count /
hud_mask_source read None -- not False -- in all 805 recorded rows of
results/outer_loop_scored_path_lever_ab_llm_on_20260726.json. The cause was NOT
that the scored path fails to compute them: hud_mask_diagnostics() is reachable
from E3AgentPolicy.explorer and the NESTED copy under row["lever2_hud_fire"] is
populated in all 805 (598 True / 207 False). The harness wrote them ONLY nested
while the sibling harness experiment_5836_frontier_discipline_ab.run_cell writes
them FLAT at row top level, so each schema's readers saw None on the other's rows.
Nothing was unmeasured; it was unreadable at the address the readers use.

The mirror-image half, also on real data: analyze_scored_path_lever_ab's
recomputed_lever2_fired read the nested key exclusively and so returned False on
all 1713 flat-schema rows of results/cptb_20260726_cells/*.jsonl.gz.

FIX. One projection (hud_row_fields) emits both addresses from a single read of the
diagnostics, wired into run_cell AND its crash path; an auditable back-fill at the
analyser's single row-entry chokepoint makes already-recorded rows readable without
re-running GPU cells; a schema/predicate-version census per arm.

A MISSING hud_shipped_mask_digest IS UNKNOWN, NOT None. digest != None is true for
every resolved mask, so reading an unrecorded key as None would arithmetically
force "fired" on 1058 of those 1713 cptb rows with no shipped-side comparison ever
happening. Guarded in both predicates and asserted by test.

VERIFIED (real output, this commit):
- End-to-end run_cell on the scored path: r11l resolved=True cells=64
  source=edge_bar_detector_req5960_stage2_confirmed digest=fcbba0b6818499b6
  shipped=None readable=True fired=True; tn36 61 cells fired=True; lp85
  resolved=False cells=0 readable=True fired=False -- a TRUE NEGATIVE now
  distinguishable from unread. Crash path also populates (unique_frames=0
  witnesses the non-ingest).
- Back-fill on the 805 real recorded rows: 805/805 None -> 598 True / 207 False,
  zero None, all tagged _hud_row_schema=nested_only (auditable, not silent).
  hud_diagnostics_unreadable_cells=[] in every arm.
- Fire census: 6 firing cells in every HUD-ON arm, 0 in S_minus_hud.
- The new test takes every asserted value from a live E3AgentPolicy.explorer and
  never writes a hud_mask_* key. SIX mutations were run and each fails it: flat
  keys dropped (2 failed), projection unwired (1), diagnostics replaced by a
  plausible constant stub (1), _ingest no-op i.e. the dead channel (2), analyser
  reverted to nested-only (1), missing-digest guard removed (1). Baseline restored
  md5-verified and green.
- pytest -k arc failure SETS byte-identical to a clean-HEAD control (44 == 44,
  none referencing the touched modules); passed 7685 -> 7688 = the 3 new tests.
- arc_orphan_solver_lint OK (65 modules); ruff check + format clean.

RESIDUAL, disclosed: the ingest witness (unique_frames / graph_nodes) was never in
the nested dict, so it is NOT recoverable by the back-fill for the 805 historical
rows -- it is populated on fresh rows only. For the 207 resolved=False historical
rows the surrogate witnesses states_expanded / nodes_total /
nodes_with_previous_frame / actions are all positive on 207/207, so the "no dead
channel" reading holds, but it rests on the surrogate rather than the canonical
field. hud_row_fields / hud_lever_fired are duplicated in harness and analyser; a
test asserts they agree on live data but does not prevent divergence.

NO behaviour change to any lever. No flag flipped. MAX_ACTIONS untouched. The
published artifact is now stale w.r.t. this analyser and must be rebuilt before any
number from it is cited.

